<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>How on Typophile Archive</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/tags/how/</link><description>Recent content in How on Typophile Archive</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 09 May 2014 09:38:00 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/tags/how/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Monotype’s Allan Haley will Present at HOW Design Live in Boston</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/116397/</link><pubDate>Fri, 09 May 2014 09:38:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/116397/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150322005631im_/http:/typophile.com/files/HDL-Logo-300x167_5726.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monotype’s Director of Words and Letters, Allan Haley, will Present “Typographic Master Lessons” on May 13, 2014, at 4:30 p.m., at the Hynes Convention Center.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Allan’s presentation will offer sage advice, design solutions and typographic inspiration from some of the most highly regarded design teachers and mentors, including Gail Anderson, Kit Hinrichs, DJ Stout, Michael Osborne, Carin Goldberg, Sean Anderson and Erik Spiekermann.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information on HOW Design Live, visit &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150322005631/http:/www.howdesignlive.com/" title="http://www.howdesignlive.com"&gt;http://www.howdesignlive.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
For more information on Allan’s presentation, please read the press release here &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150322005631/http:/bit.ly/1ouSdFe" title="http://bit.ly/1ouSdFe"&gt;http://bit.ly/1ouSdFe&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>generating font for hebrew, cyrillic &amp; latin1</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/103554/</link><pubDate>Tue, 04 Jun 2013 09:39:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/103554/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Hi everybody,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Im working on a font that includes latin1, hebrew and cyrillic.&lt;br&gt;
I already designed all the glyphs. Now I need to know what should I do before generating the font.&lt;br&gt;
I know is a big question, Im sorry, Im really lost in this step.&lt;/p&gt;
